            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Salix myrsinifolia, known as the dark-leaved willow or myrsine-leaved willow, is a species of willow native to Europe and Western Siberia. It forms a {{convert|2|-|5|m|ft|abbr=on}} high shrub. In the north, it often becomes a tree up to {{convert|8|m|ft|abbr=on}} tall."
